#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:222
msgid ""
"The equations for the kinematic viscosities of the two coagulants prepared "
"from granules are given below."
msgstr ""
"Las ecuaciones para las viscosidades cinemáticas de los dos coagulantes "
"preparados a partir de gránulos se muestran a continuación."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:224
msgid ""
"\\nu_{Alum} = \\left[ 1 + 4.225 \\times {10}^{-6}{\\left( "
"\\frac{C_{Alum}}{\\frac{kg}{m^3}} \\right)}^{2.289} \\right] \\nu_{{H_2}O}\n"
"\n"
"\\nu_{PACl} = \\left[ 1 + 2.383 \\times "
"{10}^{-5}\\left(\\frac{C_{PACl}}{\\frac{kg}{m^3}} \\right)^{1.893} \\right] "
"\\nu_{{H_2}O}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:230
msgid ""
"This analysis is incomplete in that we don't know the aluminum concentration"
" of these coagulant solutions."
msgstr ""
"Este análisis es incompleto en el sentido de que no conocemos la "
"concentración de aluminio de estas soluciones coagulantes."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:239
msgid "internal figure"
msgstr "Figura interna"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:239
msgid ""
"The viscosity of solutions prepared from granular aluminum sulfate and "
"polyaluminum chloride. The concentration is the mass of granules per volume "
"of solution."
msgstr ""
"La viscosidad de las soluciones preparadas a partir de sulfato de aluminio "
"granular y cloruro de polialuminio. La concentración es la masa de gránulos "
"por volumen de solución."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:241
msgid "Notes:"
msgstr "Notas:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:243
msgid ""
"Nothing in life is perfect, and the CDC is no exception. It has a few causes"
" of inaccuracy which go beyond non-zero minor losses:"
msgstr ""
"Nada en la vida es perfecto, y el CDC no es una excepción. Tiene algunas "
"causas de inexactitud que van más allá de las pérdidas menores distintas de "
"cero:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:245
msgid ""
"Float valves are not perfect. There will still be minor fluctuations of the "
"fluid level in the CHT which will result in imperfect dosing."
msgstr ""
"Las válvulas de flotador no son perfectas. Aún habrá pequeñas fluctuaciones "
"en el nivel de fluido en el CHT, lo que resultará en una dosificación "
"imperfecta."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:246
msgid ""
"Surface tension may resist the flow of chemicals from the dosing tube into "
"the drop tube during low flows. Since the CDC design does not consider "
"surface tension, this is a potential source of error."
msgstr ""
"La tensión superficial puede resistir el flujo de productos químicos desde "
"el tubo dosificador hacia el tubo de gota durante bajos caudos. Dado que el "
"diseño CDC no tiene en cuenta la tensión superficial, esto es una posible "
"fuente de error."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:247
msgid ""
"The lever and everything attached to it are not weightless. Changing the "
"dose of coagulant or chlorine means moving the slider along the lever. Since"
" the slider and tubes attached to it (drop tube, dosing tube) have mass, "
"moving the slider means that the torque of the lever is altered. This means "
"that the depth that the float is submerged is changed, which affects "
":math:`\\Delta h` of the system. This can be remedied by making the float’s "
"diameter as large as possible, which makes these fluctuations small. This "
"problem can not be avoided entirely."
msgstr ""
"La palanca y todo lo que está conectado a ella no son ingrávidos. Cambiar la"
" dosis de coagulante o cloro implica mover el deslizador a lo largo de la "
"palanca. Como el deslizador y los tubos conectados a él (tubo de caída, tubo"
" dosificador) tienen masa, mover el deslizador cambia el par de la palanca. "
"Esto implica que la profundidad a la que el flotador está sumergido cambia, "
"lo que afecta a :math:`\\Delta h` del sistema. Esto se puede solucionar "
"aumentando al máximo el diámetro del flotador, lo que hace que estas "
"fluctuaciones sean pequeñas. Este problema no se puede evitar del todo."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:252
msgid "Design Equations for the Linear Chemical Dose Controller (CDC)"
msgstr "Ecuaciones de diseño para el controlador lineal de dosis química (CDC)"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:253
msgid ""
"This document will include the equation derivations required to design a CDC"
" system. The most important restriction in this design process is "
"maintaining linearity between head :math:`h` and flow :math:`Q`, which is "
"the entire purpose of the CDC. Recall that major losses under laminar flow "
"scale with :math:`Q` and minor losses scale with :math:`Q^2` Since it is "
"impossible to remove minor losses from the system entirely, we will simply "
"try to make minor losses very small compared to major losses. The CDC does "
"this by including ‘dosing tube(s),’ which are long, straight tubes designed "
"to generate a lot of major losses. There can be one tube or multiple, "
"depending on the design conditions."
msgstr ""
"Este documento incluirá las derivaciones de ecuaciones necesarias para "
"diseñar un sistema CDC. La restricción más importante en este proceso de "
"diseño es mantener la linealidad entre la :math:`h` de altura y el flujo "
":math:`Q`, que es el propósito principal del CDC. Recuerda que las pérdidas "
"mayores bajo flujo laminar escalan con :math:`Q` y las menores escalan con "
":math:`Q^2` Dado que es imposible eliminar por completo las pérdidas menores"
" del sistema, simplemente intentaremos hacer que las pérdidas menores sean "
"muy pequeñas en comparación con las mayores. El CDC hace esto incluyendo "
"'tubos/los dosificadores', que son tubos largos y rectos diseñados para "
"generar muchas pérdidas mayores. Puede haber un tubo o varios, dependiendo "
"de las condiciones de diseño."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:255
msgid ""
"We will use the ‘head loss trick’ that was introduced in the Fluids Review "
"section. Therefore, the elevation difference between the water level in the "
"constant head tank (CHT) and the end of the tube connected to the slider, "
":math:`\\Delta h`, is equal to the head loss between the two points, "
":math:`h_L`. Thus, :math:`\\Delta h = h_L = h_e + h_f`."
msgstr ""
"Usaremos el 'truco pérdida de carga ' que se introdujo en la sección de "
"Revisión de Fluidos. Por lo tanto, la diferencia de elevación entre la nivel"
" del agua en el tanque de carga constante (CHT) y el extremo del tubo "
"conectado al deslizador, :math:`\\Delta h`, es igual a la pérdida de carga "
"entre los dos puntos, :math:`h_L`. Así, :math:`\\Delta h = h_L = h_e + h_f`."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:265
msgid "CDC Derivation"
msgstr "Derivación CDC"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:265
msgid "Visual representation of CDC."
msgstr "Representación visual de los CDC."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:267
msgid ""
"**When designing the CDC, there are a few parameters which are picked and "
"set initially, before applying any equations. These parameters are:**"
msgstr ""
"**Al diseñar el CDC, hay algunos parámetros que se seleccionan y establecen "
"inicialmente antes de aplicar cualquier ecuación. Estos parámetros son:**"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:269
msgid ""
":math:`D` = tube diameter. only certain tubing diameters are manufactured "
"(like :math:`\\frac{x}{16}` inch), so an array of available tube diameters "
"is set initially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:270
msgid ""
":math:`\\sum K` = sum of minor loss coefficients for the whole system. This "
"is also set initially, it is usually 2."
msgstr ""
":math:`\\sum K` = suma de los coeficientes de pérdida menor para todo el "
"sistema. Esto también se establece inicialmente, normalmente es 2."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:271
msgid ""
":math:`h_{L_{max}}` = maximum elevation difference between CHT water level "
"and outlet of solution. This parameter is usually 20 cm."
msgstr ""
":math:`h_{L_{max}}` = diferencia máxima de elevación entre el nivel del agua"
" CHT y la salida de la solución. Este parámetro suele ser de 20 cm."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:273
msgid ""
"We begin by defining the head loss through the system :math:`h_L`, which is "
"equivalent to defining the driving head :math:`\\Delta h`. Major losses will"
" be coded as red."
msgstr ""
"Comenzamos definiendo la pérdida de carga a través del sistema :math:`h_L`, "
"lo que equivale a definir la cabeza de conducción :math:`\\Delta h`. Las "
"pérdidas mayores se codificarán en rojo."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:275
msgid ""
"\\color{red}{\n"
"   h_{\\rm{f}} = \\frac{128\\nu LQ}{g\\pi D^4}\n"
"   }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:282
msgid ""
":math:`\\nu` = kinematic viscosity *of the solution going through the dosing"
" tube(s)*. This is either coagulant or chlorine"
msgstr ""
":math:`\\nu` = viscosidad cinemática *de la solución que pasa por el(los) "
"tubo(s) dosificador(es)*. Esto es coagulante o cloro"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:283
msgid ":math:`Q` = flow rate through the dosing tube(s)"
msgstr ":math:`Q` = caudal a través del(los) tubo(s) dosificador(es)"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:284
msgid ":math:`L` = length of the dosing tube(s)"
msgstr ":math:`L` = longitud del(los) tubo(s) dosificador(es)"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:286
msgid ""
"‘Tube(s)’ is used because there may be 1 or more dosing tubes depending on "
"the particular design."
msgstr ""
"Se utiliza 'tubo(s)' porque puede haber 1 o más tubos de dosificación "
"dependiendo del diseño particular."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:288
msgid "Minor losses are equal to:"
msgstr "Las pérdidas menores son equivalentes a:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:290
msgid "h_e = \\frac{8 Q^2}{g \\pi^2 D^4} \\sum{K}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:294
msgid ""
"Therefore, the total head loss is a function of flow, and is shown in the "
"following equation."
msgstr ""
"Por lo tanto, el pérdida de carga total es función del flujo, y se muestra "
"en la siguiente ecuación."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:296
msgid ""
" h_L(Q) =\n"
" {\\color{red}{\n"
"\\frac{128\\nu L Q}{g \\pi D^4}}} +\n"
"\\frac{8Q^2}{g \\pi^2 D^4} \\sum K"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:303
msgid ""
"Blue will be used to reference *actual* head loss from now on. This is the "
"same equation as above."
msgstr ""
"El azul se usará para referenciar la pérdida de carga *real* a partir de "
"ahora. Esta es la misma ecuación que la anterior."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:305
msgid ""
"\\color{blue}{\n"
"   h_L(Q) = \\left( \\frac{128\\nu L}{g \\pi D^4} + \\frac{8Q}{g \\pi ^2 "
"D^4} \\sum{K} \\right) Q\n"
"   }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:311
msgid ""
"This equation is not linear with respect to flow. We can make it linear by "
"turning the variable :math:`Q` in the :math:`\\frac{8Q}{g \\pi ^2 D^4} "
"\\sum{K}` term into a constant. To do this, we pick a maximum flow rate of "
"coagulant/chlorine through the dose controller, :math:`Q_{max}`, and put "
"that into the term in place of :math:`Q`. The term becomes "
":math:`\\frac{8Q_{max}}{g \\pi ^2 D^4} \\sum{K}`, and our linearized model "
"of head loss, coded as green, becomes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:313
msgid ""
"\\color{green}{\n"
"   h_{L_{linear}}(Q) = \\left( \\frac{128\\nu L}{g \\pi D^4} + "
"\\frac{8Q_{max}}{g \\pi ^2 D^4} \\sum{K} \\right) Q\n"
"   }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:319
msgid ""
"Here is a plot of the three colored equations above. Our goal is to minimize"
" the minor losses in the system; to bring the red and blue curves as close "
"as possible to the green one."
msgstr ""
"Aquí tienes un gráfico de las tres ecuaciones de colores anteriores. Nuestro"
" objetivo es minimizar las pequeñas pérdidas en el sistema; acercar las "
"curvas roja y azul lo más posible a la verde."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:328
msgid "CDC linearity model"
msgstr "Modelo de linealidad CDC"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:328
msgid ""
"MathCAD generated graph for linearity error analysis. TODO: make this in "
"python"
msgstr ""
"MathCAD generó un gráfico para el análisis de errores de linealidad. "
"PENDIENTE: haz esto en python"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:331
msgid "Designing for the Error Constraint"
msgstr "Diseño para la restricción de error"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:332
msgid ""
"The first step in the design is to make sure that major losses far exceed "
"minor losses. This will result in an equation for the maximum velocity that "
"can go through the dosing tube(s), :math:`{\\bar v_{max} }`."
msgstr ""
"El primer paso en el diseño es asegurarse de que las pérdidas mayores "
"superen con creces las pérdidas menores. Esto dará lugar a una ecuación para"
" la velocidad máxima que puede pasar por el(los) tubo(s) dosificador(es), "
":math:`{\\bar v_{max} }`."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:334
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Minor losses will never be 0, so how much error in our linearity are we "
"willing to accept? Let’s define a new parameter, :math:`\\Pi_{Error}`, as "
"the maximum amount of error we are willing to accept. We are ok with 10% "
"error or less, so :math:`\\Pi_{Error} = 0.1`."
msgstr ""
"Las pérdidas menores nunca serán 0, así que ¿cuánto error en nuestra "
"linealidad estamos dispuestos a aceptar? Definamos un nuevo parámetro, "
":math:`\\Pi_{Error}`, como la cantidad máxima de error que estamos "
"dispuestos a aceptar. Estamos de acuerdo con un error del 10% o menos, así "
"que :math:`\\Pi_{Error} = 0.1`."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:336
msgid ""
"\\Pi_{Error} = \\frac{\\color{green}{ h_{L_{linear}} } - \\color{blue}{ h_L "
"}}{\\color{green}{ h_{L_{linear}} }} = 1 - \\frac{\\color{blue}{ h_L "
"}}{\\color{green}{ h_{L_{linear}} }}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:340
msgid ""
"1 - \\Pi_{Error} = \\frac{\\color{blue}{ h_L }}{\\color{green}{ "
"h_{L_{linear}} }}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:344
msgid ""
"Now we plug :math:`\\color{blue}{ h_L(Q) }` and :math:`\\color{green}{ "
"h_{L_{linear}} }` back into the equation for :math:`1 - \\Pi_{Error}` and "
"take the limit as :math:`Q \\rightarrow 0`, as that is when the relative "
"difference between actual head loss and our linear model for head loss is "
"the greatest."
msgstr ""
"Ahora insertamos :math:`\\color{blue}{ h_L(Q) }` y :math:`\\color{green}{ "
"h_{L_{linear}} }` de nuevo en la ecuación para :math:`1 - \\Pi_{Error}` y "
"tomamos el límite como :math:`Q \\rightarrow 0`, ya que es cuando la "
"diferencia relativa entre la pérdida de carga real y nuestro modelo lineal "
"para pérdida de carga es mayor."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:346
msgid ""
" 1 - \\Pi_{Error} =\n"
"\\frac{ \\color{blue}{\n"
"\\left( \\frac{128 \\nu L}{g \\pi D^4} +\n"
"\\cancel{\\frac{8Q}{g \\pi^2 D^4} \\sum{K}}\n"
"\\right) Q\n"
"   }}\n"
"   {\\color{green}{\n"
"\\left( \\frac{128 \\nu L}{g \\pi D^4} + \\frac{8 Q_{max}}{g \\pi^2 D^4} "
"\\sum{K} \\right) Q\n"
"   }}\n"
"   =  \\frac{\\left( \\frac{128 \\nu L}{g \\pi D^4} \\right)}{\\left( "
"\\frac{128 \\nu L}{g \\pi D^4} + \\frac{8 Q_{max}}{g \\pi^2 D^4} \\sum{K} "
"\\right)}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:359
msgid ""
"The next steps are algebraic rearrangements to solve for :math:`L`. This "
":math:`L` describes the *minimum* length of dosing tube necessary to meet "
"our error constraint at *maximum* flow. Thus, we will refer to it as "
":math:`L_{min, \\, \\Pi_{Error}}`."
msgstr ""
"Los siguientes pasos son reordenamientos algebraicos para resolver "
":math:`L`. Este :math:`L` describe la longitud *mínima* del tubo de "
"dosificación necesaria para cumplir nuestra restricción de error en el flujo"
" *máximo*. Por tanto, lo denominaremos :math:`L_{min, \\, \\Pi_{Error}}`."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:361
msgid ""
"\\left( 1 - \\Pi_{Error} \\right)  \\frac{128 \\nu L}{g \\pi D^4} + \\left( "
"1 - \\Pi_{Error} \\right) \\frac{8 Q_{max}}{g \\pi ^2 D^4} \\sum{K}  =  "
"\\frac{128 \\nu L}{g \\pi D^4}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:365
msgid ""
"- \\Pi_{Error} \\frac{128 \\nu L}{g \\pi D^4} + \\left( 1 - \\Pi_{Error} "
"\\right) \\frac{8 Q_{max}}{g \\pi^2 D^4} \\sum{K}  = 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:369
msgid ""
"L = \\left( \\frac{1 - \\Pi_{Error}}{\\Pi_{Error}} \\right) "
"\\frac{Q_{max}}{16 \\nu \\pi} \\sum{K}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:373
msgid ""
"L_{min, \\, \\Pi_{Error}} = L = \\left( \\frac{1 - "
"\\Pi_{Error}}{\\Pi_{Error}} \\right) \\frac{Q_{max}}{16 \\nu \\pi} \\sum{K}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:377
msgid "Note that this equation is independent of head loss."
msgstr "Nótese que esta ecuación es independiente de pérdida de carga."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:379
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, both :math:`L_{min, \\, \\Pi_{Error}}` and :math:`Q_{max}` "
"are unknowns. We can plug this equation for :math:`L_{min, \\, "
"\\Pi_{Error}}` back into the head loss equation at maximum flow, which is "
":math:`h_{L_{max}} = \\left( \\frac{128\\nu L Q_{max}}{g \\pi D^4} + "
"\\frac{8Q_{max}^2}{g \\pi ^2 D^4} \\sum{K} \\right)` and rearrange for "
":math:`Q_{max}` to get:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:381
msgid ""
"Q_{max} = \\frac{\\pi D^2}{4} \\sqrt{\\frac{2 h_{L_{max}} g "
"\\Pi_{Error}}{\\sum K }}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:385
msgid ""
"**Function in aguaclara** ``cdc.max_linear_flow(Diam, HeadlossCDC, "
"Ratio_Error, KMinor)`` Returns the maximum flow :math:`Q_{max}` that can go "
"through a dosing tube will making sure that linearity between head loss and "
"flow is conserved."
msgstr ""
"**Función en aguaclara** ``cdc.max_linear_flow(Diam, HeadlossCDC, "
"Ratio_Error, KMinor)`` Devuelve el flujo máximo :math:`Q_{max}` que puede "
"pasar por un tubo dosificador, asegurando que la linealidad entre pérdida de"
" carga y flujo se conserve."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:387
msgid ""
"From this equation for :math:`Q_{max}`, we can get to our first design "
"equation, :math:`{\\bar v_{max}}` by using the continuity Equation "
":math:`\\bar v_{max} = \\frac{Q_{max}}{\\frac{\\pi D^2}{4}}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:389
msgid "\\bar v_{max} = \\sqrt{ \\frac{2 h_L g \\Pi_{Error}}{\\sum{K} }}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:395
msgid "Designing for Head Loss"
msgstr "Diseñando para pérdida de carga"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:396
msgid ""
"The second step in the design is to make sure that the maximum head loss "
"corresponds to the maximum flow of chemicals. This will result in an "
"equation for the length of the dosing tube(s), :math:`{L_{min}`."
msgstr ""
"El segundo paso en el diseño es asegurarse de que el pérdida de carga máximo"
" corresponda al flujo máximo de productos químicos. Esto dará lugar a una "
"ecuación para la longitud del(los) tubo(s) dosificador(es), "
":math:`{L_{min}`."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:398
msgid ""
"We previously derived an equation for the minimum length of the dosing "
"tube(s), :math:`L_{min, \\, \\Pi_{Error}}`, which was the minimum length "
"needed to ensure that our linearity constraint was met. This equation is "
"shown again below, in red:"
msgstr ""
"Anteriormente derivamos una ecuación para la longitud mínima del(los) "
"tubo(s) dosificador(es), :math:`L_{min, \\, \\Pi_{Error}}`, que era la "
"longitud mínima necesaria para asegurar que se cumpliera nuestra restricción"
" de linealidad. Esta ecuación se muestra de nuevo a continuación, en rojo:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:400
msgid ""
"\\color{red}{\n"
"   L_{min, \\, \\Pi_{Error}} = \\left( \\frac{1 - "
"\\Pi_{Error}}{\\Pi_{Error}} \\right) \\frac{Q_{max}}{16 \\nu \\pi} \\sum{K}"
"\n"
"   }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:406
msgid ""
"This equation does not, however, account for getting to the proper amount of"
" head loss. If we were to use this equation to design the dosing tubes, we "
"might not end up with the proper amount of flow :math:`Q_{max}` at the "
"maximum head loss :math:`h_{L{max}}`. So we need to double check to make "
"sure that we get our desired head loss."
msgstr ""
"Sin embargo, esta ecuación no tiene en cuenta cómo se alcanza la cantidad "
"adecuada de pérdida de carga. Si usáramos esta ecuación para diseñar los "
"tubos de dosificación, podríamos no obtener la cantidad adecuada de flujo "
":math:`Q_{max}` en el máximo pérdida de carga :math:`h_{L{max}}`. Por eso "
"necesitamos comprobar dos veces que obtenemos la pérdida de carga deseada ."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:408
msgid ""
"First, consider the head loss at maximum flow that was used to get the "
"equation for :math:`Q_{max}`:"
msgstr ""
"Primero, consideremos la pérdida de carga en el flujo máximo que se utilizó "
"para obtener la ecuación para :math:`Q_{max}`:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:410
msgid ""
"h_{L_{max}} = \\left( \\frac{128 \\nu L{Q_{max}}}{g \\pi D^4} + \\frac{8 "
"Q_{max}^2}{g \\pi^2 D^4} \\sum{K} \\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:414
msgid ""
"Now that we know all of the parameters in this equation except for "
":math:`L`, we can solve the equation for :math:`L`. This the *shortest* tube"
" that generates our required head loss, :math:`h_{L_{max}}`."
msgstr ""
"Ahora que conocemos todos los parámetros de esta ecuación excepto :math:`L`,"
" podemos resolver la ecuación para :math:`L`. Este es el tubo *más corto* "
"que genera nuestro pérdida de carga requerido , :math:`h_{L_{max}}`."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:417
msgid ""
"\\color{green}{\n"
"   L_{min, \\, head loss} = L = \\left( \\frac{g h_{L_{max}} \\pi D^4}{128 "
"\\nu Q_{max}} - \\frac{Q_{max}}{16 \\pi \\nu} \\sum{K} \\right)\n"
"   }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:423
msgid ""
"**Function in aguaclara:** ``cdc._length_cdc_tube_array(FlowPlant, "
"ConcDoseMax, ConcStock, DiamTubeAvail, HeadlossCDC, temp, en_chem, KMinor)``"
" Returns :math:`{L_{min}`, takes in the flow rate input of *plant design "
"flow rate*."
msgstr ""
"**Función en aguaclara:** ``cdc._length_cdc_tube_array(FlowPlant, "
"ConcDoseMax, ConcStock, DiamTubeAvail, HeadlossCDC, temp, en_chem, KMinor)``"
" Devuelve :math:`{L_{min}`, toma la caudal entrada de *diseño de plantas "
"caudal*."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:425
msgid ""
"**Function in aguaclara:** ``cdc._len_tube(Flow, Diam, HeadLoss, conc_chem, "
"temp, en_chem, KMinor)`` Returns :math:`{L_{min}`, takes in the flow rate "
"input of *max flow rate through the dosing tube(s)*."
msgstr ""
"**Función en aguaclara:** ``cdc._len_tube(Flow, Diam, HeadLoss, conc_chem, "
"temp, en_chem, KMinor)`` Devuelve :math:`{L_{min}`, recibe la entrada caudal"
" de *max caudal a través del(los) tubo(s) de dosificación*."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:427
msgid ""
"If you decrease the max flow :math:`Q_{max}` and hold :math:`h_{L_{max}}` "
"constant, :math:`\\color{green}{L_{min, \\, head loss}}` becomes larger. "
"This means that a CDC system for a plant of 40 :math:`\\frac{L}{s}` must be "
"different than one for a plant of 20 :math:`\\frac{L}{s}`. If we want to "
"maintain the same head loss at maximum flow in both plants, then the dosing "
"tube(s) will need to be a lot longer for the 20 :math:`\\frac{L}{s}` plant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:429
msgid ""
"To visualize the distinction between :math:`\\color{red}{  L_{min, \\, "
"\\Pi_{Error}}}` and :math:`\\color{green}{ L_{min, \\, head loss}}`, see the"
" following plot. :math:`\\color{green}{ L_{min, \\, head loss}}` is "
"discontinuous because it takes in the smallest allowable tube diameter as an"
" input. As the chemical flow rate through the dosing tube(s) decreases, the "
"dosing tube diameter does as well. Whenever you see a jump in the green "
"points, that means the tubing diameter has changed."
msgstr ""
"Para visualizar la diferencia entre :math:`\\color{red}{  L_{min, \\, "
"\\Pi_{Error}}}` y :math:`\\color{green}{ L_{min, \\, head loss}}`, véase el "
"siguiente gráfico. :math:`\\color{green}{ L_{min, \\, head loss}}` es "
"discontinuo porque recibe el diámetro más pequeño permitido del tubo como "
"entrada. A medida que el químico caudal a través del(los) tubo(s) "
"dosificador(es) disminuye, el diámetro del tubo dosificador también "
"disminuye. Cada vez que ves un salto en los puntos verdes, eso significa que"
" el diámetro del tubo ha cambiado."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:438
msgid "CDC length model"
msgstr "Modelo de longitud CDC"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:438
msgid "CDC length modeling in MathCAD."
msgstr "Modelado de longitud CDC en MathCAD."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:440
msgid ""
"As you can see, the head loss constraint is more limiting than the linearity"
" constraint when designing for tube length. Therefore, the design equation "
"for tube length is the one which accounts for head loss. This is the second "
"and final design equation for designing the CDC:"
msgstr ""
"Como puedes ver, la restricción de pérdida de carga es más limitante que la "
"restricción de linealidad al diseñar para la longitud del tubo. Por lo "
"tanto, la ecuación de diseño para la longitud del tubo es la que tiene en "
"cuenta pérdida de carga. Esta es la segunda y última ecuación de diseño para"
" diseñar el CDC:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:442
msgid ""
"L_{min} = L_{min, \\, head loss} = \\left( \\frac{g h_{L_{max}} \\pi "
"D^4}{128 \\nu Q_{max}} - \\frac{Q_{max}}{16 \\pi \\nu} \\sum{K} \\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:448
msgid ""
"The equations for :math:`\\bar v_{max}` and :math:`L_{min}` are the only "
"ones you **need** to manually design a CDC."
msgstr ""
"Las ecuaciones para :math:`\\bar v_{max}` y :math:`L_{min}` son las únicas "
"que **necesitas** para diseñar manualmente un CDC."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:452
msgid "Designing for Dosing Tube Diameter"
msgstr "Diseño para el diámetro del tubo de dosificación"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:453
msgid ""
"Below are equations which also govern the CDC and greatly aid in "
"understanding the physics behind it, but are not strictly necessary in "
"design."
msgstr ""
"A continuación se muestran ecuaciones que también rigen el CDC y ayudan "
"mucho a entender la física que hay detrás de ellas, pero no son "
"estrictamente necesarias en el diseño."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:455
msgid ""
"By rearranging :math:`Q_{max} = \\frac{\\pi D^2}{4} \\sqrt{\\frac{2 h_L g "
"\\Pi_{Error}}{\\sum K }}`, we can solve for :math:`D` to get the *minimum* "
"diameter we can use assuming the shortest tube possible that meets the error"
" constraint, :math:`\\color{red}{L_{min, \\, \\Pi_{Error}}}`. If we use a "
"diameter smaller than :math:`D_{min, \\, \\Pi_{Error}}`, we will not be able"
" to simultaneously reach :math:`Q_{max}` and meet the error constraint "
":math:`\\Pi_{Error}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:457
msgid ""
"\\color{blue}{\n"
" D_{min, \\, \\Pi_{Error}} = \\left[ \\frac{8 Q_{max}^2 \\sum "
"K}{\\Pi_{Error} h_l g \\pi^2} \\right]^{\\frac{1}{4}}\n"
" }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:463
msgid ""
"We can also find the minimum diameter needed to guarantee laminar flow, "
"which is another critical condition in the CDC design. We can do this by "
"combining the equation for Reynolds number at the maximum :math:`\\rm{Re}` "
"for laminar flow, :math:`{\\rm{Re}}_{max} = 2100` with the continuity "
"equation at maximum flow:"
msgstr ""
"También podemos encontrar el diámetro mínimo necesario para garantizar el "
"flujo laminar, que es otra condición crítica en el diseño del CDC. Podemos "
"hacer esto combinando la ecuación para el número de Reynolds en el "
":math:`\\rm{Re}` máximo para el flujo laminar, :math:`{\\rm{Re}}_{max} = "
"2100` con la ecuación de continuidad en el flujo máximo:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:465
msgid "{\\rm Re}_{max}  = \\frac{\\bar v_{max} D}{\\nu}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:469
msgid "\\bar v_{max} = \\frac{4 Q_{max}}{\\pi D^2}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:473
msgid "To get:"
msgstr "Para conseguir:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:475
msgid ""
"\\color{red}{\n"
" D_{min, \\, Laminar} = \\frac{4 Q_{max}}{\\pi \\nu {\\rm{Re}}_{max}}\n"
" }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:481
msgid ""
"Combined with the discrete amount of tubing sizes (shown in dark green), we "
"can create a graph of the three diameter constraints:"
msgstr ""
"Combinado con la cantidad discreta de tamaños de tubería (mostrada en verde "
"oscuro), podemos crear un gráfico de las tres restricciones de diámetro:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:490
msgid "CDC diameter model"
msgstr "Modelo de diámetro CDC"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Derivations.rst:490
msgid "CDC diameter modeling in MathCAD."
msgstr "Modelado de diámetros CDC en MathCAD."

